# INPUT01 evidence: zView started from EmuDESK (fs09 prep-card kind zv2:
# NEWDESK.INF restores the window C:\ZVIEW\, ZVIEW.NAP at (63,165)), and the
# pointer is moved WITHOUT a pause while zView loads its codecs: from tick 886
# one 2-px step every 2 ticks (10 ms), zig-zag x 100..500 at y 300, until tick
# 2886 (10 s). The first move waits until 880 -- past the double-click window
# (a move of more than 2 px inside it closes the gesture at the NEW position,
# EmuTOS mchange, and the double click would land on the empty desktop). Every step line on the serial log carries its scheduled tick
# (sched) and the tick it really ran (at): the lag is the time the input pump
# did not run. B_DCLICK triggers the screendump burst (drive-m3.py --burst).
# Then File > Quit like deskzv2 (fs09) and END. Ticks hz_200 after
# "[desk] desktop up" (desk-arm-m3.py).
